<h1 class="heading-title heading-title--separated">About Paul Smith</h1>

<p>I’m Paul, a lead interaction designer at NHS England, based just outside Manchester.</p>

{% imgr {
    imagePath: 'content/about-photo.jpeg',
    alt: 'Paul stood in front of a room full of people presenting about the DWP Design System',
    width: '800',
    height: '400',
    quality: '90'
  }
%}

<p>I have over 20 years’ experience designing and building digital products and services. I work with researchers, clinicians, developers and other designers to understand problems, test ideas and make services easier to use.</p>
<p>My background combines interaction design and frontend development. I use code to prototype ideas, and I care about accessibility and how a service works beyond an individual screen.</p>
<p>At NHS England, I work on urgent and emergency care services, including NHS 111 online. I’m exploring how AI-assisted navigation can help people find the care they need, and how to make those interactions understandable.</p>
<p>I also mentor designers and contribute to the NHS Design System, NHS Prototype Kit and NHS Frontend. I enjoy helping teams share what they learn and giving other designers room to develop their own judgement.</p>
<p>Earlier roles have included work with the BBC, DWP, the National Lottery Heritage Fund and the planning data team. My <a href="/weeknotes/">weeknotes</a> are where I reflect on work and life as they happen.</p>

